17592186725728 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725652 1079 #uuid "8efe075d-4034-5877-9e2e-551be0608d3d" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725653 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725731 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725653 1071 "**(a)** Derive a separable differential equation involving $\\theta$, $v$, and $dv/d\\theta$. Show the change of variable." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725653 1072 #uuid "8f2ff586-5c08-5985-851b-11eed9fd9327" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725653 1074 "Here $v$ is angular velocity. The change to angle as the independent variable is local where that parametrization is valid; omitting the chain-rule factor $v$ gives the wrong equation." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725654 1080 "-6" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725654 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725654 1083 #uuid "906c3a2f-1636-53a2-9793-95133477f785" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725655 1062 #uuid "91bf3383-307c-5078-ae2f-1f2d7f3916ff" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725655 1063 #edb/ref 17592186725594 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725656 1058 #edb/ref 17592186725619 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725656 1062 #uuid "92bd04ad-ba70-561a-9f88-acc676653321" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725656 1063 #edb/ref 17592186725607 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725657 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725588 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725657 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725657 1077 "age" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725657 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725588 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725657 1079 #uuid "92f69073-39c9-540a-88f2-910dd52db0c0" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725658 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725681 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725658 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725700 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725658 1071 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 7](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_3/7).\n\nThe general solution of $y\\!\\prime\\!\\prime+2y\\prime-24y=0$ has the form $y(x)=c_1e^{r_1x}+c_2e^{r_2x}$. Find $r_1$ and $r_2$.\n\n$r_1=$ {{r1}} and $r_2=$ {{r2}}." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725658 1072 #uuid "931f5d2e-4962-5c0e-b914-226502af5591" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725658 1074 "The characteristic polynomial is $r^2+2r-24=(r-4)(r+6)$, so the two roots are $4$ and $-6$. One labeling is $r_1=4$, $r_2=-6$; reversing the labels gives the same general solution after swapping $c_1,c_2$. The two roots must be distinct." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725659 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725562 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725659 1071 "**(c)** Solve the IVP to determine $Q(t)$. $Q(t)=$ {{mass}} pounds.\n\nNotation: $e^z=\\exp(z)$ denotes the natural exponential." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725659 1072 #uuid "955723f3-9c6b-53de-8450-decddf9985a5" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725659 1074 "The equilibrium mass is $30$ pounds. Set $U=Q-30$ to get $U\\prime=-U/15$, $U(0)=-15$, so $Q=30-15e^{-t/15}$. Check $Q(0)=15$ and $Q\\prime=e^{-t/15}=2-Q/15$." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725660 1062 #uuid "95e39026-d6ca-5077-b8d2-f53a5bdb2044" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725660 1063 #edb/ref 17592186725587 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725643 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725661 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725661 1077 "temperature" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725661 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725643 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725661 1079 #uuid "9673354b-2210-5191-b893-0af62d3dbe3f" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725662 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725554 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725662 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725662 1077 "work" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725662 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725554 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725662 1079 #uuid "96d5f7d5-ae7a-5cb7-bc2a-a29131601489" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725663 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048391 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725663 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048774 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725663 1089 #edb/ref 17592186725658 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725663 1090 #uuid "971c582b-668b-59b4-8767-c64c8908b194" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725664 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725723 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725664 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725664 1077 "rhs" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725664 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725723 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725664 1079 #uuid "9b713f2e-8b2d-53a6-a765-d17b9de42731" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725665 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725580 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725665 1071 "**(d)** Solve $P(t)=100000$ for $t$ to determine the time to reach that population. $t=$ {{time}} hours." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725665 1072 #uuid "9c3f031f-f0e2-55e2-880e-f5857e2be6b4" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725665 1074 "$2000e^{rt}=100000$ reduces to $e^{rt}=50$. Therefore $t=\\ln50/r=10\\ln50/\\ln10\\approx16.9897$ hours after the initial observation." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725666 1080 "\\frac{Q}{120}" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725666 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725666 1083 #uuid "9c44a045-ff98-5251-b665-a6b6049c4b06" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725697 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] 