bWork_3/6).\n\nFor what values of $r$ does $y=e^{rx}$ satisfy $y\\!\\prime\\!\\prime-9y\\prime+20y=0$? Separate the values by commas: $r=$ {{roots}}." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725672 1072 #uuid "a39e7c4b-5b0d-5e36-8919-5cac9904beee" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725672 1074 "Substitution gives $e^{rx}(r^2-9r+20)=0$. Since the exponential never vanishes, solve $(r-4)(r-5)=0$, giving $r=4,5$. Substituting either value into the characteristic polynomial gives zero." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725673 1080 "\\frac{\\ln 10}{10}" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725673 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725673 1083 #uuid "a586136b-925b-5997-a73b-a6dd624e954a" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725674 1080 "The initial energy is $E_0=m/2+9k/8$. Draw the ellipse $kx^2+mv^2=m+9k/4$ through $(-1.5,1)$. Its horizontal semiaxis is $\\sqrt{9/4+m/k}$ and vertical semiaxis is $\\sqrt{1+9k/(4m)}$. Mark the initial point in the upper-left quadrant and clockwise motion. The initial tangent is $(x\\prime,v\\prime)=(1,3k/(2m))$, pointing right and up. The exact aspect ratio depends on the unspecified $k/m$." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725674 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725674 1083 #uuid "a7d48639-3eee-59ba-8b4a-2662888d849f" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725676 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725675 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725675 1077 "work" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725675 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725676 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725675 1079 #uuid "a844a431-31cd-5553-9c7b-7ee6f5c2a820" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725676 1080 "Integrating $v\\,dv=-g\\sin\\theta\\,d\\theta$ gives $v^2/2=g\\cos\\theta+C$. Thus $v^2/2+g(1-\\cos\\theta)=C+g=E$, after renaming 