7592186502323 true] [17592186725721 1083 #uuid "e39301a8-3c31-5a77-a7fb-459d8c254cd3" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725722 1080 "The chain rule gives $\\theta\\!\\prime\\!\\prime=(dv/d\\theta)(d\\theta/dt)=v\\,dv/d\\theta$. Hence $v\\,dv/d\\theta=-g\\sin\\theta$, equivalently $v\\,dv=-g\\sin\\theta\\,d\\theta$." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725722 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725722 1083 #uuid "e619384c-0826-5b03-8089-28d199da7636" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725723 1080 "2-\\frac{Q}{15}" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725723 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725723 1083 #uuid "e6aa4002-f1ac-51f1-b8a9-d92e79d5cf46" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725724 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725609 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725724 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725620 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725724 1071 "**(d)** Forget the initial conditions in (c). For the physical mass, assume $m>0$. Solve the energy equation in (b) for $v$ in terms of $x$, then replace $v$ by $dx/dt$ to obtain a first-order ODE with constants $m,k,E$. Give both branches.\n\n$v=$ {{v}}; $\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=$ {{rhs}}." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725724 1072 #uuid "e6ef7d7a-fd29-5796-b3a0-dfabf1ed28a9" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725724 1074 "Rearrange to $mv^2=2E-kx^2$, then take both square roots. Real motion requires $2E-kx^2\\geq0$ when $m>0$. Each sign describes a monotone segment; a nonconstant oscillation changes branches at turning points. This is not one fixed-sign equation for the entire oscillation." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725725 1080 "$y_1\\prime=e^x$ and $y_2\\prime=(1+x)e^x$. Hence $W=\\begin{vmatrix}e^x&xe^x\\\\e^x&(1+x)e^x\\end{vmatrix}=e^{2x}\\ne0$ on $\\mathbb R$. Both are solutions and the equation has continuous coefficients on $\\mathbb R$. The Wronskian proves linear independence, so these two solutions form a fundamental set on $\\mathbb R$." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725725 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725725 1083 #uuid "e70a42d6-a4a8-5bb2-a355-4ffaecd94e70" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1043 #edb/ref 17592186725542 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1043 #edb/ref 17592186725568 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1043 #edb/ref 17592186725599 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1043 #edb/ref 17592186725632 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1043 #edb/ref 17592186725640 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1045 "MTH 256 — R-5" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1046 #edb/ref 17592186725640 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1047 #inst "2026-10-29T06:59:00.000Z" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1048 #edb/ref 17592186405205 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725726 1053 #uuid "e7b84f66-042b-5d51-8a92-685449650428" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725727 1080 "\\pm\\sqrt{2E-2g\\cdot(1-\\cos\\theta)}" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725727 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725727 1083 #uuid "e9b48a54-b8ca-5358-9f48-69a5d0aec979" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725728 1080 "\\frac{\\ln(17/12)}{10}" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725728 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725728 1083 #uuid "eea4edcd-2fab-535c-b25e-687557e78beb" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725729 1058 #edb/ref 17592186725604 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725729 1062 #uuid "ef165eb9-eb31-5161-a8f8-f018cf34d636" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725729 1063 #edb/ref 17592186725618 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725730 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725593 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725730 1071 "**(c)** Draw three trajectories in the $\\theta$–$v$ plane: (i) rocking motion, (ii) counterclockwise rotating motion, and (iii) clockwise rotating motion. Choose initial conditions corresponding to each type.\n\n![Source pendulum phase plane](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FWHW-3%2Fpendulum-phase-plane.png)" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725730 1072 #uuid "f036f5f1-7a77-54ec-9788-b8c52978888e" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725730 1074 "The potential energy ranges from $0$ to $2g$. Thus $0<E<2g$ gives rocking, $E>2g$ gives rotation, and $E=2g$ is the separatrix, not a generic rotation. The upper and lower rotation branches never meet because $v$ never vanishes. Physical rotation direction is the sign of angular velocity; it is distinct from the orientation of a closed curve in the phase plane." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725722 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725731 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725731 1077 "work" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725731 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725722 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725731 1079 #uuid "f1983a61-fc77-544e-91a4-b0bdb9d27db5" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725732 1062 #uuid "f21949c6-dc20-50d1-8532-a5dee0c24e65" 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725732 1063 #edb/ref 17592186725572 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725733 1068 #edb/ref 17592186725627 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725733 1071 "**(b)** When will the thermometer read $0^\\circ C$? Time $=$ {{time}} minutes after it was taken outdoors." 13194139542354 17592186502323 true] [17592186725733 1072 #uuid "f2c3e3f6-f5b2-54c1-b03d-5a605d6a1530" 13194139542354 17592186502323 tru